# The door contracts this repo's CI holds its door to: parachute-core `contracts/suites/door` at an exact commit
# (T-431). One suite runs against every way of running Parachute (a box, this hosted door, a personal Cloudflare
# door); `scripts/door-parity.sh` runs it here against both workers under local workerd and compares the result with
# the box's kept fingerprint in that same commit (`contracts/suites/door/golden/`).
#
# This pin is separate from the engine pin (core-source.env) on purpose. The contracts are black-box: they speak HTTP
# and MCP and import nothing from the engine, and they know which release line a door is on. So this pin can follow
# parachute-core `next` while the engine this door runs stays where core-source.env holds it.
#
# Moving it: bump the SHA in its own change and run `bash scripts/door-parity.sh`. A new difference is either drift
# in this door (fix it here) or a difference meant on both sides (name it in parachute-core
# `contracts/suites/door/deliberate.json`, with why and who decides).
DOOR_SUITE_REPO_URL="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute-core.git"
DOOR_SUITE_REF="6d7a0458987b30457683ab799f18d018776172fb"
# The box fingerprint this door is compared with (a file in contracts/suites/door/golden/ at that commit).
DOOR_SUITE_GOLDEN="box-0.8"
